   "lang": "python",
   "code": "class Solution:\n    def romanToInt(self, s: str) -> int:\n        # Map each Roman numeral symbol to its integer value\n        hashtable = {\n        'I': 1,\n        'V': 5,\n        'X': 10,\n        'L': 50,\n        'C': 100,\n        'D': 500,\n        'M': 1000\n        }\n\n        # Running total\n        res = 0\n\n        # Loop through every character except the last one.\n        # We stop before the last character because we compare s[i]\n        # with the character immediately after it: s[i + 1].\n        for i in range(len(s) - 1):\n\n        # If the current Roman numeral is smaller than the next one,\n        # it represents subtraction.\n        # Examples:\n        # IV = 5 - 1 = 4\n        # IX = 10 - 1 = 9\n        # XC = 100 - 10 = 90\n        # CM = 1000 - 100 = 900\n        # So if current < next, subtract the current value from res.\n        if hashtable[s[i]] < hashtable[s[i + 1]]:\n        res -= hashtable[s[i]]\n\n        # Otherwise, this numeral is being used normally,\n        # so add its value to the running total.\n        else:\n        res += hashtable[s[i]]\n\n        # The loop never processes the final character because there is\n        # no character after it to compare against.\n        res += hashtable[s[-1]]\n\n        return res",
   "notes": "# Mechanism\nThe code looks at each Roman numeral and compares it to the one after it.\n\nIf the current value is smaller than the next one, subtract it: (because it represents a 9 or a 4 in roman numeral syntax)\n\n```text\nIV is 4 in roman numeral syntax, but algo doesnt know that, so check:\nIV = I and V, -> 1 and 5, since 1 < 5 because 1 - 5 = -4 (negative),\nit must be 5 - 1 = 4\n```\n\nIf the current value is not smaller, add it normally: (default case, not 9 or 4)\n\n```text\nVI → 5 > 1\n+5 +1\n= 6\n```\n\nSo the rule is:\n\n```python\nif current < next:\n    subtract current\nelse:\n    add current\n```\n\nThe last character gets added separately because there is no character after it to compare with.",
