   "code": "class Solution:\n    def climbStairs(self, n: int) -> int:\n        # Edge case: if there's only 1 step, there's only 1 way\n        if n <= 1:\n            return 1\n        # 1. Create the notebook (size n + 1 so index matches step number)\n        dp = [0] * (n + 1)\n        # 2. Base cases (what we know upfront)\n        dp[1] = 1  # 1 way to reach step 1: (1)\n        dp[2] = 2  # 2 ways to reach step 2: (1+1) or (2)\n        # 3. Fill the notebook step-by-step from step 3 up to n\n        for i in range(3, n + 1):\n            dp[i] = dp[i - 1] + dp[i - 2]\n        # 4. Your final answer is sitting right at dp[n]\n        return dp[n]",
