   "notes": "I only made 1 mistake which was:\n\nYour bug is here:\n\n```python\nif self.min > value:\n```\n\nWhen you push another value equal to the current minimum, like the second `0`, you do not save the old minimum.\n\nSo after popping that `0`, your stack restores the previous minimum as `2`, even though another `0` is still in the stack.\n\nChange it to:\n\n```python\nif self.min >= value:\n```\n\nSo equal minimums are also tracked:\n\n```python\ndef push(self, value: int) -> None:\n    self.storage.append(value)\n    if self.min >= value:\n        self.prevMin.append(self.min)\n        self.min = value\n```\n\nThat fixes the duplicate minimum case.",
